<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">10 events that happened on 4 February, from 960 to 2004.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">960 <span class="tih-ago">1,066 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zhao Kuangyin founds the Song dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Proclaimed emperor by his troops at Chenqiao, the general became Emperor Taizu of Song. The dynasty reunited most of China and presided over remarkable advances in commerce, printing and technology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Emperor Taizu of Song</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1789 <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Electors unanimously choose George Washington as President</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Presidential electors cast their votes and every one named George Washington. He remains the only President to win every electoral vote, which he did again in 1792.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-domingue.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1794 <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French National Convention abolishes slavery</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Inspired by the slave revolt in Saint-Domingue, the Convention abolished slavery in all French colonies. Napoleon restored it in 1802, and France did not abolish it finally until 1848.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1801 <span class="tih-ago">225 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Marshall becomes Chief Justice of the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marshall began 34 years as Chief Justice, the longest in the Court's history. His rulings, beginning with Marbury v. Madison, established judicial review and a strong federal government.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1861 <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Seceded states meet at Montgomery to form the Confederacy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from six seceded states opened a convention in Montgomery, Alabama. Within days they adopted a provisional constitution and chose Jefferson Davis as provisional President.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1899 <span class="tih-ago">127 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philippine-American War breaks out in Manila</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shots exchanged between American and Filipino troops sparked war between the United States and the Philippine Republic. Officially ended in 1902, the conflict killed some 200,000 or more Filipino civilians.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1938 <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler takes personal command of the German armed forces</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After forcing out War Minister Blomberg and army chief Fritsch on trumped-up charges, Hitler abolished the War Ministry and assumed direct command. Ribbentrop became Foreign Minister the same day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-nations.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yalta Conference opens in Crimea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Churchill, Roosevelt and Stalin met at the Livadia Palace to plan the end of the war. They agreed on the occupation of Germany, elections in Poland, Soviet entry into the Pacific war and the United Nations.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sri-lanka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1948 <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ceylon becomes independent from Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ceylon became a self-governing dominion in the Commonwealth, ending about 150 years of British rule. It became a republic and took the name Sri Lanka in 1972.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2004 <span class="tih-ago">22 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mark Zuckerberg launches 'TheFacebook' at Harvard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Harvard student launched a social network for fellow students. Opened to the public in 2006, Facebook grew to billions of users and transformed how people share news and personal life.</p></div></li></ol>
